    "html": "<p>* note: this project is ongoing as freelance design work</p><p>the griffin is a automated blood sample pathogen detection platform.</p><p>&gt; designing the enclosure for the griffin with internal airflow channels and vent placement to guide cooling air across electronics and peltier thermal subsystems.&nbsp;</p><p>&gt;&nbsp;optimized the housing for mass production using injection molding: added draft, consistent wall thickness, and mold-friendly split lines while keeping a clean exterior form.</p><p>&gt; incorporated snap-fits and minimal fasteners to simplify assembly and service, reducing part count and assembly steps for scalable manufacturing.</p>",
